BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Paint Your Pet! A Watercolor Workshop
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260624T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260624T120000
UID:260620QWqBYlyR9U20F53_-b8_Kg
DESCRIPTION:Buy an All Access Pass here. \n\nBuy a Lecture Pass here.\n\nF
 or Ages: 18\\+\n\nCapture the spirit of your beloved companion in this eng
 aging watercolor pet portrait workshop. Using a favorite photo as your ref
 erence\, you'll learn how to translate fur\, expression\, and personality 
 into luminous layers of color through guided demonstrations and personaliz
 ed instruction. Building on core watercolor techniques&mdash\;like keen ob
 servation\, color mixing\, and value&mdash\;you'll develop your compositio
 n step by step with patient\, intentional washes. Perfect for all skill le
 vels\, this class combines technical skill-building with heartfelt creativ
 ity\, resulting in a portrait that feels both vibrant and deeply personal.
  \n\nThis workshop is located in the classroom.\n\nAbout the Teacher: \n\n
 Hannah Day is a multidisciplinary artist based in Sonoma County\, working 
 primarily on paper. She holds a BA in Visual Arts from the University of S
 an Diego and an MFA in printmaking from the University of Hawaii at Manoa.
  Her internationally exhibited etchings are complemented by work in paper 
 cutting\, graphite\, and watercolor. Exploring the fragile ways we perceiv
 e reality\, her work invites viewers into a liminal space between terror a
 nd awe. Hannah has over a decade of teaching experience and currently teac
 hes watercolor and observational drawing at local arts organizations throu
 ghout Sonoma County. \n\nLearn more about Hannah:\n\nwww.hannahdrawstrees.
 com@hannah\\_day\\_art
LOCATION:Petaluma Arts Center
URL:https://mynorthbaytickets.ticketsauce.com/e/pacacademy-paint-your-pet?
 aff=cityspark
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Exploring Color
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260624T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260624T160000
UID:260610z1aUQhAsSUGjj-MnBxfWjA
DESCRIPTION:Buy an All Access Pass here. \n\nBuy a Lecture Pass here.\n\nF
 or Ages: 13\\+\n\nIn this 3-hour workshop\, participants will explore the 
 fundamentals of color theory using acrylic paint\, starting with the prima
 ry colors and expanding into a rich spectrum of hues through guided color 
 mixing. Students will experiment with blending\, gradation\, and observing
  how colors interact\, discovering a wide range of tones and subtle variat
 ions between them. Through playful exploration and simple exercises\, the 
 workshop encourages curiosity\, confidence\, and a deeper understanding of
  how color can be used for expression. No prior painting experience is nec
 essary&mdash\;this accessible\, hands-on workshop welcomes participants of
  all levels to engage with color in a meaningful and creative way.\n\nThis
  workshop is located in the classroom.\n\nAbout the Teacher: \n\nEsther Hi
 lsenrad is a Bay Area&ndash\;based artist and educator originally from New
  York City\, with over 23 years of teaching experience across a wide range
  of subjects and age groups. Her career has spanned formal classroom teach
 ing\, museum education\, and work as a teaching artist. Now working indepe
 ndently\, Esther teaches art camps from her home studio\, afterschool art 
 classes\, and private lessons for elementary-aged children. Her deepest pa
 ssion lies in art education&mdash\;guiding others to feel confident expres
 sing themselves creatively and exploring diverse artistic mediums. In her 
 own artistic practice\, Esther enjoys experimenting with color theory thro
 ugh acrylic painting\, crafting miniature scenes from recycled materials\,
  and creating jewelry and other crafts. Her work is driven by a genuine lo
 ve of both making art and helping others discover their creative voice.\n\
 nTo learn more about Esther:\n\nwww.esthertheartteacher.com\n\nww.estherhe
 artsart.com\n\n@esthertheartteacher\n\n@estherheartsart
LOCATION:Petaluma Arts Center
URL:https://mynorthbaytickets.ticketsauce.com/e/pacacademy-exploring-color
 ?aff=cityspark
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
