BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Mom's Club
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260625T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260625T200000
UID:260531KJ7F5c1UMke2PTZkiMEzBQ
DESCRIPTION:SummaryWhen a surge of extremist candidates takes over their l
 ocal school boards\, a group of suburban moms &mdash\; fierce\, funny\, an
 d fed up &mdash\; launches a covert resistance to defend their LGBTQ\\+ ki
 ds and protect public education. Armed with open-source intelligence\, &ld
 quo\;sock puppet&rdquo\; accounts\, and a Signal chat that turns into a di
 gital command center\, these unlikely activists uncover a chilling conspir
 acy: their communities are battlegrounds in a decadeslong war led by a sec
 retive network of religious extremists and billionaires bent on dismantlin
 g the public school system.Told with the urgency of a true crime thriller 
 and the heart of a grassroots uprising\, Moms Club is a defiant\, deeply p
 ersonal story of resistance. This is not just a film about school board dr
 ama -  it's a battle cry for democracy\, inclusion\, and the future of our
  children.\n\nYour ticket donation goes to fund Wake UP Sonoma and the Mom
 's Club Impact Campaign\n\nSPONSORED BY:   \n\nThe Moms Club Impact Campai
 gn is a nationwide communityengagement initiative designed to expand the c
 onversationsurrounding public education\, misinformation\, politicalextrem
 ism\, LGBTQ\\+ inclusion\, and grassroots organizing.Through screenings\, 
 educational resources\, advocacy efforts\,digital outreach\, and community
  partnerships\, the campaignaims to empower audiences with tools\, informa
 tion\, andactionable pathways for civic engagement.At its core\, the campa
 ign is about helping communities betterunderstand the forces shaping publi
 c education whilesupporting individuals and organizations working to prote
 ctdignity\, inclusion\, and democratic participation at the local level.\n
 \nCO DIRECTORS\n\nMiranda Winters &amp\; Rocky Romano are the creative for
 ce behind Winters Rock\, an award-winning Los Angeles-based production com
 pany celebrated for its striking and thought-provoking nonfiction content.
  Focused on the vast capabilities and inherent limits of the human spirit\
 , their work delivers engaging narratives that are both locally grounded a
 nd globally significant. Their expertise in storytelling coupled with a bo
 ld cinematic style provides audiences with an intimate look into diverse\,
  tight-knit\, and often underrepresented communities around the world. The
 ir narratives have spanned from the streets of Los Angeles\, as seen in th
 eir award-winning short films We Can't Breathe \\(2020\\) and Gangsta Gard
 ener \\(2024\\)\, to the adrenaline-inducing waves of Portugal and Hawaii\
 , showcased in the Emmy award-winning HBO series The 100 Foot Wave and Red
  Chargers \\(2017\\)\, to the vast plains of Wyoming filming wild horses f
 or their feature documentary Blue Zeus \\(2025\\)\, narrated by Gerard But
 ler\, which won the Audience Award for Best Documentary at the 2025 Newpor
 t Beach Film Festival.Miranda &amp\; Rocky are committed to creating socia
 lly conscious projects that tell meaningful stories about the forces shapi
 ng our lives.
LOCATION:Sebastiani Theatre
URL:https://mynorthbaytickets.ticketsauce.com/e/moms-club?aff=cityspark
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
