SUMMARY:Teja Gerken & Adam Miller - Innovative Guitar x2!
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260626T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260626T213000
UID:260617h9ZbEE1TwkuTkUOeRg7cDw
DESCRIPTION:Australian fingerstyle guitar master Adam Miller joins Marin c
 ounty's own Teja Gerken for an evening of guitar magic at the Fairfax Barb
 ershop! The barbershop?? Yes\, the barbershop at 67 Broadway in downtown F
 airfax\, California hosts one of the Bay Area's coolest occasional undergr
 ound music series\, and if you get there early\, you even get to sit in on
 e of the vintage chairs!\n\nTEJA GERKEN & ADAM MILLER Friday\, June 26\, 7
 PM Live a the Fairfax Barbershop 67 Broadway\, Fairfax\, California Email 
 spencervergara@yahoo.com for info \\(415\\) 258-0178 $20 suggested donatio
 n\n\nWith a career spanning just over 20 years\, ADAM MILLER had early beg
 innings as a solo guitar virtuoso\, that led to session playing\, producin
 g\, mix & master engineer\, university educator\, and everything in betwee
 n\, but his vision of creating instrumental guitar music has never lost fo
 cus. He has toured the globe\, performing in the USA\, Canada\, UK\, Germa
 ny\, France\, Italy\, Denmark\, The Netherlands\, Sweden\, Poland\, Japan\
 , Australia & even Afghanistan for the Australian and Allied Forces. Mille
 r has shared stages with Les Paul\, Tommy Emmanuel\, Samantha Fish\, Mike 
 Stern\, Charlie Hunter\, Tomo Fujita\, Adam Levy\, Matt Schofield\, Mason 
 Stoops\, Molly Miller\, Josh Smith\, Joey Landreth\, Russell Morris\, Arie
 l Posen\, Tony McManus\, Ben Gillies \\(Silverchair\\)\, Chris Cheney \\(T
 he Living End\\) amongst so many others. With glowing coverage in guitar &
  music press around the world\, the 2002 Australian Fingerstyle Guitar Cha
 mpion even has his own signature model guitar from Nik Huber Guitars.\n\nw
 ww.adammiller.com.au\n\nSan Francisco Bay Area guitarist TEJA GERKEN has e
 nchanted audiences ever since coming onto the acoustic fingerstyle scene i
 n the late 1990s. Teja presents a program that reflects his diverse musica
 l interests\, with a typical set including originals\, Celtic traditionals
 \, classical pieces\, jazz standards\, and some favorite tunes by his fing
 erstyle guitar peers. Teja’s piece “Takoma” won the instrumental cat
 egory of the 2025 USA Songwriting competition\, and Acoustic Guitar magazi
 ne called his most recent album Test of Time\, “A sonic marvel\, from to
 p to bottom.”\n\n“Gerken’s technical facility is obvious\, his perfo
 rmances impeccable\, and his tones gorgeous” – Barry Cleveland\, guit
 arplayer.com.\n\nwww.tejagerken.com See less
LOCATION:Fairfax Barber Shop
URL:https://www.facebook.com/events/2090756258168895/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
