BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Pride Print Lab - Trace Monotype with Ash Hay
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260626T173000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260626T193000
UID:260607FIGfDFVXZUy38pbQQpaMRA
DESCRIPTION:Date & Time\n\nFriday\, June 26\, 2026\n\n5:30 PM – 7:30 PM\
 n\nLocation\n\nRoom 208\n\nCategory\n\nPrintmaking\n\nExperience Level\n\n
 All Levels\n\nAges\n\nAll Ages\n\nAdult Registration Cost:\n\n$15\n\nUnder
  15 Registration Cost:\n\nFree\n\nTotal Registration Cost:\n\n$15\n\nCeleb
 rate Pride at Print Lab with Ash Hay! Learn trace monotype printmaking in 
 this social art workshop. No experience needed\, create art to take home.\
 n\nprogram overview\n\nRoll up your sleeves and join us for a fun Print La
 b evening celebrating Pride Month\, with special guest\, Ash Hay – one o
 f our featured June Causeway Gallery artists! Print Lab is not a tradition
 al class\, but an affordable art-making experience. Our mission is to expl
 ore a creative arts technique socially with our community. We welcome you 
 to print\, play and experiment with an activity to create something unique
  in our printmaking studio! This month we will explore a fun printmaking t
 echnique known as Trace Monotype.  Trace monotypes involve drawing direct
 ly onto an inked plate and do not require the use of a press! The pressure
  of the pencil transfers the ink to the paper\, creating a soft look to pr
 ints with unlimited options. Guests will learn about the variety of mark m
 aking\, and explore expressive textures on an inky surface.  Ash Hay will
  give a short artist talk\, and teach the basics of creating trace monotyp
 es\, a printmaking process they enjoy using to create prints. They will sh
 are their process of incorporating layered prints\, as well as utilizing m
 ixed media. Come join us\, make some monotypes to take home\, and explore 
 the possibilities!  Enjoy light refreshments during this printmaking acti
 vity. No previous experience is necessary!
LOCATION:Sonoma Community Center
URL:https://sonomacommunitycenter.org/programs/pride-print-lab/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Sister Act
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260626T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260626T220000
UID:260604wL7MTZw2bk2odcbhfRztmA
DESCRIPTION:Sister Act is the high-energy musical comedy based on the belo
 ved 1992 film. Featuring an electrifying Alan Menken score infused with di
 sco and gospel beats\, this feel-good show is a celebration of music\, sis
 terhood\, and second chances. When disco diva Deloris Van Cartier witnesse
 s a crime\, she’s forced into hiding—in a convent! Disguised as a nun\
 , she transforms the struggling choir with her powerhouse voice\, helping 
 them find their sound while discovering her own. Nominated for five Tony A
 wards\, Sister Act is a joyful\, soul-stirring spectacle that proves music
 —and a little mischief—can work miracles
LOCATION:6th Street Playhouse
URL:https://www.facebook.com/events/907119495682865/907119509016197/?activ
 e_tab=about
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Wreckless Strangers and Pardon the Interruption at The California 
 Theater
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260626T200000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260626T200000
UID:260602aEpBHBGCzUS53u0DUnuRbA
DESCRIPTION:Fueled by national radio airplay and a climb up the Top 50 Ame
 ricana and AAA Singles charts\, Wreckless Strangers continue celebrating
  the release of their new album\, Dirty Souls\, with a summer run of per
 formances across the greater Bay Area. Newly announced dates include The 
 California Theater in Santa Rosa \\(with Pardon the Interruption\\) on J
 une 26\, the Point Richmond Outdoor Music Series on July 10\, the 4th 
 Annual Valley Car Show in Woodacre on July 18\, The Barn in Gilroy on
  July 19\, Live on the Avenue in San Anselmo on August 22\, the Old
  Western Saloon in Point Reyes Station on August 28\, the  Rio Nido R
 oadhouse on August 30 with stops in Colorado and Wyoming along the wa
 y!\n\nWith Dirty Souls\, Wreckless Strangers return to their rock-and-rol
 l roots\, delivering their rawest and most visceral studio effort to date.
  The six-song collection channels the arena rock spirit of the ’70s and 
 ’80s that shaped the band’s earliest influences while bringing a fresh
 \, modern edge to the sound. The first single\, "Dirty Soul\," released J
 anuary 23\, is receiving national airplay and is available on major stream
 ing platforms. The band released the full album on March 27.
LOCATION:The California
URL:https://www.caltheatre.com/event-details/wreckless-strangers-and-pti
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
