BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Back pOrchEstra: American Roots at Waterhawk Lake Club 6/26\, Fri 
 5:00-8:00
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260626T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260626T200000
UID:260623mpxwGCxqaUGvuFuq5SkPOQ
DESCRIPTION:Back pOrchEstra: American Roots show at Waterhawk Lake Club Ju
 ne 26\, Fri 5:00-8:00pm\n\nJoin us for... some Indie and roots rock and th
 e American Roots that inspired it... with Candy Girard\, Tim Eschliman\, G
 ary Potterton\, Jen Rund and Luis Rodriguez in a mostly-acoustic format on
  resonator guitar\, violin\, bass\, drums\, percussion\, dobro & Telecaste
 r...\n\nWe have a single out!: https://orcd.co/lxz1l6v "I'm Wild About My 
 Lovin'"\, celebrating the new "Stories In The Heart" album\, listen now!: 
 https://orcd.co/5xga7nr\n\nThe Neo-Motown/Levon Helm style single\, "Ever 
 Think About It\," is here: https://orcd.co/qo5579q\n\nLPs\, CDs\, and USB-
 Music Cards available all over\, including https://www.globerecords.com\n\
 nVince's Hot Picks (Best of 2026): "... a warm\, road-worn album that lean
 s into rich acoustic tones while freely bending genres without ever breaki
 ng the feel. Built around a mostly unplugged framework\, the record draws 
 from country blues\, roots rock\, Zydeco\, Tex-Mex\, New Orleans rhythms\,
  Motown soul\, singer-songwriter traditions\, and even Brazilian textures\
 , all woven together with an easy confidence that sounds earned\, not asse
 mbled."\n\nWaterhawk Lake Club 5000 Roberts Lake Road\, Rohnert Park\, CA\
 , 94928. A lake club for the rest of us. Perched on the edge of a small la
 ke with a sprawling outdoor space\, serving craft cocktails and reimagined
  American classics - all with a side of sunshine and good company.\n\nBack
  pOrchEstra has songs from all over the map... originals and reworked clas
 sics by Hank Williams\, Taj Mahal\, Dan Hicks\, Big Bill Broonzy\, Bob Wil
 ls\, Jimmy Reed\, Joseph & Cleome Falcon and Bobby Charles.\n\nwhat a samp
 le? check out the "Dusty Road I'm On" video: https://youtu.be/jj0IIkUyrE4 
 ...a twangy roots rock number with a Cajun flavor and hints of Jesse Ed Da
 vis and Sid Page....\n\n"...everything from alt. rock to cajun\, to countr
 y\, to Brownie Ford era Western Swing. But the thing that keeps this set t
 ogether is their excellent songwriting full of smooth never-miss-a-beat li
 nes and vivid imagery. It's a studio album but it sure does have a back po
 rch jam band feel to it" - Calvin Powers\, WHUP-FM\, americanamusicshow.co
 m\,\n\nmore at... https://www.BackpOrchEstra.com\n\nBandCamp: https://back
 porchestra.bandcamp.com\n\nyouTube: https://www.youtube.com/playlist?list=
 PLOTwG2XEiO2O8c0dEI-7hlpI8nr7apiNf\n\nBluesky: https://bsky.app/profile/ba
 ckporchestra.bsky.social\n\nReverb Nation: https://www.reverbnation.com/ba
 ckporchestra\n\nFacebook: https://www.facebook.com/BackPorchEstra/\n\nInst
 agram: https://www.instagram.com/backporchestra/\n\n#rootsrock\n\n#america
 nrootsmusic\n\n#americanamusic\n\n#rockabillymusic\n\n#twangyguitar\n\n#ba
 ckporchestra\n\n#acousticmusic\n\n#adultalbumalternative\n\n#singersongwri
 ter\n\n#folkmusic\n\n#folkrock
LOCATION:Waterhawk Lake Club
URL:https://www.BackpOrchEstra.com/shows.html
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Bongs + Books Silent Book Club at The Lounge at Mercy
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260626T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260626T200000
UID:260623NEqCR2t4uUOVwIgbNVoYeQ
DESCRIPTION:Because sometimes the best kind of community… is quiet.🌿
 📖\n\nNo assigned books\, no deadlines\, no discussions you have to part
 icipate in — just a shared space to unwind\, light up\, and get lost in 
 a good read. Bring whatever you’re currently reading (or listening to - 
 we have coloring books and puzzles for our audiobook lovers!)\, grab somet
 hing to smoke\, and settle in for a cozy night of uninterrupted reading al
 ongside fellow book lovers.\n\nCome solo or with friends and enjoy comfy v
 ibes\, good weed\, and a room full of people happily minding their own bus
 iness.\n\nHow it works:\n\n5-6pm: Arrive\, get settled\, and kick things o
 ff with a short welcome sesh.\n\n6-7pm: Uninterrupted reading time\, lo-fi
  music\, and chill energy.\n\n7-8pm: wrap up chapters\, meet other readers
 \, one last sesh to end the evening!
LOCATION:The Lounge at Mercy
URL:https://bookclubs.com/bongs-books-silent-book-club/join/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
