SUMMARY:Sundays in the Plaza: David Correa Trio (Latin / World Guitar)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260628T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260628T150000
UID:260528nQD1aRXELkiS6hklt4Geqg
DESCRIPTION:Join us for a series of relaxing afternoons in the plaza this 
 summer from 1:00 PM - 3:00 PM. Each week will feature a live music perform
 ance from a local band or performer. Not to be confused with Tuesdays in t
 he Plaza\, this is a great opportunity to bring a picnic\, sit back\, rela
 x and enjoy the melodies.\n\nAbout the band: Based in the San Francisco Ba
 y Area\, David Correa is a national recording and touring artist on Baja/T
 SR Records. Correa and his band have been entertaining audiences since 199
 9 with its passionate and distinctive blend of instrumental Latin Guitar W
 orld Fusion. Blending the Spanish guitar with Afro-Cuban and Latin rhythms
  from Mexico & Central America and a hint of middle-eastern influenced mel
 odies.
LOCATION:Healdsburg Plaza
URL:https://healdsburg.gov/899/Sundays-in-the-Plaza
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Little Shop of Horrors
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260628T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260628T140000
UID:260528e23nXh2XOUOEeAjW19qvSg
DESCRIPTION:Howard Ashman and Alan Menken gave the world this camp classic
  in 1982. They based musical (loosely) on the low-budget 1960 black comedy
  film *The Little Shop of Horrors*\, with Menken’s score featuring spec
 tacular music: early 1960s-style rock and roll\, doo-wop\, and early Motow
 n.\n\nThe story centers on meek floral assistant Seymour Krelborn\, who st
 umbles across a new breed of plant he names “Audrey II” after his cowo
 rker crush. This foul-mouthed\, R&B-singing carnivore promises unending fa
 me and fortune to the down-and-out Krelborn as long as he keeps feeding it
  BLOOD. Over time\, though\, Seymour discovers Audrey II’s out-of-this-w
 orld origins and its intent toward global domination!\n\n**June 26\, 27\, 
 28\; July 2\\*\, 3\, 5\, 9\, 10\, 11\, 12**\n\n**Friday and Saturday Shows
 :** 7:30 PM\n\n**Sunday Matinee:** 2:00 PM\n\n**\\*Value Thursday:** 7:30 
 PM\n\nBook and Lyrics by Howard Ashman\n\nMusic By Alan Menken  \n\nDirec
 tor                  Katie Watts-Whitaker\n\nMusic Direct
 or        Kelly Considine\n\nChoreographer       Katie Watts-Wh
 itaker
LOCATION:The Raven Performing Arts Theater
URL:https://raventheater.org/events/little-shop/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Salsa and Mimosa
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260628T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260628T113000
UID:260528Gw-5fJ_T-UWMBOUVJx52pQ
DESCRIPTION:Salsa & Mimosas: A Women-Only Sunday Morning Social \n\nUnwin
 d\, move\, and connect! Join us at Salsa Dance Marin for the perfect ble
 nd of rhythm and refreshment. Get your body moving and your spirits high j
 ust in time for the weekend wrap-up.\n\nNo experience needed. This event i
 s all about fun\, community\, and treating yourself.\n\nEvent Details\n\n
 • Date: Sunday\, June 28\n\n• Time: 10:00 AM – 11:30 AM\n\n• Loc
 ation: Salsa Dance Marin 4140 Redwood Hwy\, Suite 8\, San Rafael\, CA\n\
 nWhat to Expect\n\n• 10:00 AM – 11:00 AM | Lively Salsa Class: Shake 
 off the week with a one-hour introductory salsa lesson. Our instructor wil
 l guide you through the basic steps\, turns\, and rhythm—no partner or p
 revious experience required!\n\n• 11:00 AM – 11:30 AM | Mimosas & Ming
 ling: After working up a sweat\, reward yourself! Sip on crisp\, refreshi
 ng mimosas while chatting and connecting with an incredible community of l
 ocal women.\n\nGood to Know\n\n• What to wear: Comfortable clothes you 
 can easily move in\, and shoes that allow you to spin and dance comfortabl
 y.\n\n• Who it’s for: This event is strictly Women Only. Grab your b
 est friends\, your sisters\, or come solo to meet new friends!\n\nReserve 
 Your Spot\n\nSpace is limited to ensure everyone has plenty of room on the
  dance floor.
LOCATION:Salsa Dance Marin
URL:https://salsadancemarin.com/salsa-and-mimosa/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Lavender Bloom Fest Open Farm Day
