BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Stories of the Light: Between Tide and Tower
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260628T133000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260628T153000
UID:260624VUQzJdWFz06w3h3Lzk7EzA
DESCRIPTION:Step back in time with a National Park Service interpretive ra
 nger dressed in historic lighthouse keeper attire as you explore the legac
 y of the Point Reyes Lighthouse. From the Lighthouse Observation Deck\, yo
 u’ll journey through tales both luminous and shadowed—stories of isola
 tion\, ingenuity\, family life\, and the relentless power of the sea. Look
 ing out over the vast ocean landscape at the edge-of-the-earth\, you’ll 
 see where natural forces meet human determination. Discover how this remot
 e outpost shaped the lives of its keepers\, and how their experiences cont
 inue to illuminate who we are today. This program blends history\, place-b
 ased storytelling\, and breathtaking scenery for visitors seeking a deeper
  understanding of Point Reyes’ maritime heritage. Drop-in anytime betwee
 n 1:30 PM and 3:30 PM. Programs are approximately 15 minutes long and occu
 r on a rolling basis. Make sure to bring layers\, as weather at the Point 
 Reyes Lighthouse can be variable and change quickly.  The Lighthouse Obser
 vation Deck is ADA accessible. ADA parking is available. For more informat
 ion\, please call 415-464-5100
LOCATION:Point Reyes National Seashore
URL:https://www.facebook.com/events/1342294331103889/1342294344437221/?act
 ive_tab=about
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
