BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Park Rx-Forest Bathing Walks 2026
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260628T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260628T130000
UID:260227BmyMtqtarE2HlCpsXDY4dA
DESCRIPTION:Have you heard about “Shinrin-yoku” or “forest ba
 thing”? Here is an opportunity to take a walk and experience 
 the practice for yourself. Learn techniques to maximize the healt
 h benefits and stress reducing qualities of this walking practice
 . Shinrin-yoku originated in Japan and is gaining popularity in 
 the United States for its documented health benefits. This practi
 ce takes a walk in the woods to another level. A centering and
  calming restorative practice\, it promotes balance and restored 
 vitality through a quality of presence and heightened sensory awa
 reness. Sugarloaf Ridge State Park hosts a Forest Therapy Series
  as part of its Park Rx Program the 4th Sunday of the month 
 \\(March through November\\) led by certified Association of Natur
 e and Forest Therapy \\(ANFT\\) practitioners.
LOCATION:Sugarloaf Ridge State Park
URL:https://www.pressdemocrat.com/events/#/details/park-rx-forest-bathing-
 walks-2026/17736824/2026-06-28T10
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Overeaters Anonymous (OA) Newcomer Meeting in Santa Rosa
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260628T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260628T170000
UID:260212k7lSfmMx50a74EAZA6tciw
DESCRIPTION:Is Food a Problem for You? You Are Not Alone.\n\nOvereaters An
 onymous \\(OA\\) is a fellowship of people who support each other in recov
 ering from compulsive eating and food behaviors. If you feel you have a pr
 oblem with food\, OA welcomes you—no matter what your background\, belie
 fs\, or eating habits.\n\nWe hold an in-person newcomer meeting on Sundays
  from 4:00 – 5:00 PM at Christ Church United Methodist\, 1717 Yulupa Ave
 .\, Room \\#4\, Santa Rosa. Contact: Abigail \\(707\\) 293-5888. You may v
 iew all North Bay OA in-person and online meetings at https://www.northbay
 oa.org/meetings.html .\n\nIn OA\, members experience spiritual\, emotional
 \, and physical recovery by practicing the Twelve Steps and living by thei
 r spiritual principles—one day at a time.\n\nOA is not a diet club or ca
 lorie-counting program.\n\nMembers have different plans of eating.\n\nOA d
 oes not endorse any specific food plan.\n\nIf food is causing problems in 
 your life\, you don’t have to struggle alone. Recovery is possible\, and
  help is available.\n\nVisit: https://www.northbayoa.org/\n\nFind a meetin
 g: https://www.northbayoa.org/meetings.html
LOCATION:Christ Church United Methodist
URL:https://www.northbayoa.org/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Group Rides with Sports Basement
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260628T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260628T120000
UID:260122spZheMAFlk6WrW4Y6rl63Q
DESCRIPTION:Join us every month for a group ride from Sports Basement!\n\n
 We meet on the last Sunday of the month at 9am inside the store and start 
 the ride at 9:15am.\n\nMost routes are 30-40 miles and all rides are no-dr
 op\, meaning we won’t leave any rider behind. \n\nRegular updates can b
 e found on our Strava Page \\(search for: Sports Basement Santa Rosa Rides
 \\)\n\nFeel free to call the store with any questions at 707-921-3151.\n\n
 Hope to see you there!
