BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Miss Magnolia Beaumont Goes to Provincetown
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260701T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260701T210000
UID:260617AkLPduAhrEumQLSpgtyDSQ
DESCRIPTION:WEDNESDAY AND THURSDAY\, JULY 1 AND 2 AT 7:30PM A Southern deb
 utante shares a body with a gay New Yorker—comic chaos meets Provincetow
 n magic. When Southern debutante Miss Magnolia Beatrice Devareux Beaumont 
 chokes on a pork rib\, she awakens in the body of a middle-aged\, gay New 
 Yorker—“Master Joseph”—en route to Provincetown for a birthday get
 away. What begins as shock and spirited disagreement turns into an unexpec
 ted journey of shared consciousness\, clashing perspectives\, and surprisi
 ng tenderness. More than a monologue\, Miss Magnolia Beaumont Goes to Prov
 incetown is a witty\, heartfelt solo play exploring identity\, purpose\, a
 nd the magic of Provincetown. Hailed as “rich\, wise\, and deeply human
 ” \\(Backstage\\) and “a fierce and funny fable” \\(Next Magazine\\)
 \, this charming comic fantasy celebrates the beauty of unlikely connectio
 n. LEARN MORE ABOUT JOE AND THE SHOW ON INSTAGRAM https://www.instagram.co
 m/joehutcheson/ TICKETS: PURCHASE IN ADVANCE AND SAVE! Zones A & B ensure 
 a seat. Zone C has limited seating\, plus standing room. Zone A $30 Zone B
  $25 Zone C $20 \\(does not guarantee seating\\) Tickets at the door $30 \
 \(Zone C only\\) Doors open 6:30pm.  Our kitchen serves our All New Menu f
 rom the time doors open until end of intermission. \\(Kitchen available on
 ly at events with 60 or more advance tickets sold\\)
LOCATION:The California
URL:https://www.facebook.com/events/1194379246020707/?acontext=%7B%22event
 _action_history%22%3A[%7B%22mechanism%22%3A%22lov_feed%22%2C%22surface%22%
 3A%22bookmark%22%7D]%2C%22ref_notif_type%22%3Anull%7D
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Novato Art\, Wine and Music Festival  2026
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260701T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260701T000000
UID:2606179q8mpRbUkEiQnroF2rpNDA
DESCRIPTION:Based in the San Francisco Bay Area\, Dave Sampson is a freela
 nce guitarist\, producer\, multi-instrumtentalist and music instructor. Dr
 awing from his experiences living and playing in the music scenes of Austi
 n\, Los Angeles\, Seattle\, and Memphis\, Sampson put roots down in the Ba
 y Area in 2004. Dave's vibrant and versatile style supports a wide range o
 f genres and artists. His work can be heard on a variety of records\, majo
 r films\, and national radio and television shows. Always favoring taste\,
  melody\, and finding the perfect complimentary part\, his approach to pla
 ying has been compared to Mike Campbell\, David Lindley\, Mark Knopfler\, 
 Daniel Lanois and Lindsey Buckingham.
LOCATION:Downtown Novato Center
URL:https://www.bandsintown.com/e/107918000?app_id=pkvts0on0m&came_from=28
 7&utm_medium=api&utm_source=partner_api&utm_campaign=event
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Art Exhibit: Local Color
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260701T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260701T180000
UID:260616IVejytZx7Uub2GQ8BNdflA
DESCRIPTION:Date: FOR IMMEDIATE RELEASE  6/15/26\n\n**JULY EXHIBIT: LOC
 AL COLOR**\n\nEXHIBIT DATES:  **June 29 – July 26\, 2026**\n\n**RECEPT
 ION: SATURDAY\, July 4\, 2026\, 3-6 pm: Join us to meet Linda Barretta  
 and Gallery artists\;  Learn about their art and celebrate the show.  
 Be sure to take part in the Gallery’s free monthlong drawing for a beaut
 iful work by a Gallery artist.  Refreshments will be served.**\n\nSonoma
  County artist\, **Linda Barretta** presents **Local Color\,** a collecti
 on unveiling new oil paintings that tap into the vivid natural hues found 
 in our region’s breathtaking beauty.  From flowers to vineyards\, colo
 r takes a starring role in these works.  The deep purple hills in “Sun
 flower Daze” intensify the golden sweep of the sunflowers.  A peach tr
 ee celebrates the season with a glorious pink floral display in “Spring 
 Blooms.”  In “Winery Farm and Gardens\,” framed through a natural 
 arch of trees\, a sunlit vineyard draws the viewer.  “We are so fortun
 ate to live in Sonoma wine country – it’s stunning beauty is a daily i
 nspiration to pick up my brushes and paint\,” commented Barretta. \n\nL
 iving in Healdsburg\, Sonoma wine country is Barretta’s homebase.  She
  developed her impressionist style and skills through numerous hours of pl
 ein air painting and studying with master artists.  When Barretta create
 s the composition\, she is observing the play of light and colors that wil
 l highlight the compelling quality of the scene.  Her aim is to translat
 e her inspiration to the viewer.  From the rough sketch to the final bru
 shstroke\, this is the task she loves.  Barretta participates in the Art
  Trails Open Studio program and her works are exhibited regionally and thr
 oughout the country\,\n\nMeet the artist: Barretta will host the Gallery o
 n July 4\, 6 & 26\, 2:30 – 6pm and July 22\, 11am to 2:30 pm.\n\nThe Sta
 irway Smallworks Showcase features **Beverly Bird’s Birds by Bird\,** a
  collection of acrylic paintings that depict our feathered friends\, big a
 nd small\, in natural habitats.  Rendered in an impressionistic textured
  style\, these works imbue their subjects with a lively spirit.  Bald ea
 gles leave the viewer awed with their regal presence.  While the Steller
  and Scrub jays jauntily hint at their quirky character. In “Circling th
 e Light” the viewer joins a flock of geese on its migratory path. “Bir
 ds enliven our daily existence and their wild spirit provides endless subj
 ect matter\,” Bird noted of her inspiration for the series.\n\nMeet the 
 artist: Bird will host the Gallery on July 22 & 27\, 2:30 – 6pm and July
  29\, 11am to 6 pm.\n\nAlso join us for **ART NITE HEALDSBURG**\, Thursday
 \, July 2\, 5 – 7 pm.  ART NITE Healdsburg\, held the 1st Thursday of
  Every Month\, is a community event celebrating art and creativity with ov
 er 20 galleries participating.  ArtNiteHealdsburg.com.\n\nUpstairs Art G
 allery\, 306 Center Street\, Healdsburg\, CA 95448. (707) 431-4214.: OPEN 
 DAILY: 11am – 6 pm.    **www.upstairsart gallery.net** \n\nFor furt
 her information: Contact: Beverly Bird\, Press Contact\, at bvdrio@sonic.
 net or 707-799-1490.
LOCATION:Upstairs Art Gallery
URL:http://www.upstairsartgallery.net
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Introduction to Acrylic Painting
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260701T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260701T130000
UID:260608f5eKnNMVuka9lXxCFaum-Q
DESCRIPTION:Schedule\n\nWednesdays\, June 24 – July 29\, 2026 10:00 AM 
 – 1:00 PM Exceptions: July 8 & August 5\n\nLocation\n\nRoom 208\n\nExper
 ience Level\n\nBeginning\n\nEvent Categories: Drawing & Painting\, Extende
 d Classes\n\nAge\\(s\\)\n\n18 and older\n\nRegistration Cost:\n\n$250\n\nM
 aterials Fee:\n\nIncluded\n\nTotal Registration Cost:\n\n$250\n\nJoin our 
 6-week acrylic painting course for beginners. Covers color mixing\, brush 
 techniques\, and composition across landscape and abstract styles.\n\nAbou
 t the Class\n\nThis six-week acrylic painting course is designed for begin
 ners and students with minimal experience. The class focuses on the fundam
 entals of painting\, covering basic techniques and skills\, using a variet
 y of approaches. Students will learn how to handle paint and mix colors\, 
 as well as develop composition while exploring a wide range of subject mat
 ter\, including still life\, portraiture\, abstraction\, and the landscape
 . Group discussions and slide presentations are interspersed throughout th
 e course\, as well as time for one-on-one progress reviews with the instru
 ctor. If you have been considering painting this class will open the door 
 for your exploration. Some basic drawing experience suggested. Repeat stud
 ents welcome. Upon registration the instructor will contact you about supp
 lies needed for the class.
LOCATION:Sonoma Community Center
URL:https://sonomacommunitycenter.org/programs/introduction-to-acrylic-pai
 nting/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
