BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:SCREAM at FUN SIZE Blasted Art Gallery
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260702T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260702T190000
UID:260624m5cS1LHJ1Eyf0v9-WU9QNw
DESCRIPTION:Twelve Sonoma County artists will “SCREAM” together in a m
 iniature exhibit. The exhibit\, as well as every individual artwork in the
  show share the same title: SCREAM.\n\nThe miniature FUN SIZE Blasted Art 
 Gallery\, which measures 16 x 33 x 21”\, serves as a portable vessel for
  this chorus of artists\, was created as a timely response to global\, nat
 ional\, local\, and personal issues.\n\nThese artists will be SCREAMing to
 gether: Arminée Chahbazian\, Art Moura\, Bill Shelley\, Britta Kathmeyer\
 , Carlos Perez\, Chris Beards\, Jennifer Mygatt Tatum\, Kathleen Youngquis
 t\, Keviette Minor\, Kristen Throop\, Nick Mancillas\, and Nicole Mathers.
 \n\nThe Thursday\, July 2 Grand Opening at Rena Charles Gallery \\(439 Hea
 ldsburg Ave.\, Healdsburg\\) is from 5-7pm\, coinciding with Art Nite Heal
 dsburg First Thursday.\n\nIf you miss Thursday's event\, the following nig
 ht\, Friday\, July 3 Opening Reception is at the Santa Rosa Arts Center in
  the SOFA Arts District \\(312 South A Street\, Santa Rosa\\) at 5-8pm\, c
 oinciding with SOFA Arts District First Friday. \n\nAlso see SCREAM on Sa
 turday\, July 11\, at Studio LZ Gallery in The Watershed\, \\(429 First St
 reet\, Suite 130\, Petaluma\\) at 4-7pm.\n\nThese events are free.\n\nSCRE
 AM and FUN SIZE Blasted Art Gallery are a project of Blasted Art Gallery \
 \(Santa Rosa artists Chris Beards & Bill Shelley\\)\, which presented gall
 ery exhibits featuring Sonoma County artists from 2017 to 2019 in the SOFA
  Arts District in Santa Rosa\, and online in 2020.
LOCATION:Rena Charles Gallery
URL:https://www.pressdemocrat.com/events/#/details/scream-at-fun-size-blas
 ted-art-gallery/19154704/2026-07-02T17
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Miss Magnolia Beaumont Goes to Provincetown
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260702T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260702T210000
UID:260617mUSsQS3FU0a8x8HKLQCanw
DESCRIPTION:A Southern debutante shares a body with a gay New Yorker—com
 ic chaos meets Provincetown magic. When Southern debutante Miss Magnolia B
 eatrice Devareux Beaumont chokes on a pork rib\, she awakens in the body o
 f a middle-aged\, gay New Yorker—“Master Joseph”—en route to Provi
 ncetown for a birthday getaway. What begins as shock and spirited disagree
 ment turns into an unexpected journey of shared consciousness\, clashing p
 erspectives\, and surprising tenderness. More than a monologue\, Miss Magn
 olia Beaumont Goes to Provincetown is a witty\, heartfelt solo play explor
 ing identity\, purpose\, and the magic of Provincetown. Hailed as “rich\
 , wise\, and deeply human” \\(Backstage\\) and “a fierce and funny fab
 le” \\(Next Magazine\\)\, this charming comic fantasy celebrates the bea
 uty of unlikely connection. Learn more about Joe and the show on Instagram
  https://www.instagram.com/joehutcheson/ TICKETS: PURCHASE IN ADVANCE AND 
 SAVE! Zones A & B ensure a seat. Zone C has limited seating\, plus standin
 g room. Zone A  $30 Zone B $25 Zone C $20 \\(does not guarantee seating\\)
  Tickets at the door $30 \\(Zone C only\\) Doors open 6:30pm.  Our kitchen
  serves our All New Menu from the time doors open until end of intermissio
 n. \\(Kitchen available only at events with 60 or more advance tickets sol
 d\\)
LOCATION:The California
URL:https://www.facebook.com/events/1023509423669806/1023510573669691/?act
 ive_tab=about
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
