BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Wake the Dead Concert
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260705T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260705T190000
UID:260519S1x1Kjz5AUSYIKStA5DWXw
DESCRIPTION:St. Columba’s Inverness Celtic Music Series invites you to a
 n afternoon with Wake the Dead\, The World’s Only Celtic All-Star Gratef
 ul Dead Jam Band. Enjoy live music in our beautiful outdoor amphitheater. 
 Advance tickets $25\, Children under 12 free \\($30 at door\, cash only\\)
 . Refreshments will be for sale\, including beer and wine. Doors open at 4
  pm\n\nWAKE THE DEAD is a romp that flows seamlessly from rock grooves to 
 hot Irish reels\, and from haunting airs to achingly beautiful melodies fa
 miliar to Deadheads everywhere. “Sugaree” in waltz time\, bracketed by
  an ancient harp tune and infused with a poignant Celtic longing. “Berth
 a” thundering out of “China Cat” on a mandolin tidal wave. The eerie
  lilt of the uilleann pipes\, giving a glow to “Bird Song” as if it wa
 s always meant to be there. Groove jams to keep the tie-dye swirling. Voca
 l harmonies that float like clouds. The music takes off\, and the band fol
 lows\, grinning all the way. These aren’t worlds colliding — they’re
  worlds meshing\, coalescing creating a whole new world of possibility\, a
 nd true to the spirits of the Grateful Dead and the eternally hopeful Celt
 s.\n\nWAKE THE DEAD bands together six of the best-known and most respecte
 d players in the west. Bassist Cindy Browne is equally at home in folk and
  jazz\, touring globally as the musical fusion go-to gal. Singer\, fiddler
 \, and octave mandolinist Danny Carnahan is an award-winning songwriter wh
 ose original Irish-tinged songs are popular worldwide. Sylvia Herold’s d
 elicious vocal phrasing can also be heard on her solo recordings and her p
 erformances with Euphonia. Paul Kotapish is known far and wide for his wor
 k with Kevin Burke’s Open House\, and for his blazing guitar and mandoli
 n with The Hillbillies From Mars and Euphonia. And Latin percussionist Bri
 an Rice rounds out the band’s groove engine. Valerie Rose is an accompli
 shed Irish fiddler\, singer\, and vocal arranger. She teaches at various m
 usic camps including California Coast Music Camp\, Walker Creek Music Camp
 \, and the San Francisco Irish Cultural Center’s Youth Irish Camp. She c
 onducts Palo Alto’s M’Earthtones choir and leads the Rose Tree Youth C
 eili Band and monthly Irish sessions at Redwood City’s Alhambra Irish Ho
 use. \n\nGet your tickets toady at https://www.stcolumbasinverness.org/wa
 ke-the-dead-concert
LOCATION:St. Columba's Inverness
URL:https://www.stcolumbasinverness.org/wake-the-dead
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Penngrove Parade and BBQ
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260705T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260705T160000
UID:2605197aACkzoML069Mt_T-Le8kQ
DESCRIPTION:**Stars\, Stripes\, and A Parade!** Celebrate 250 Years at the
  Penngrove Parade's 50th Parade at 11 am\, and deep pit BBQ in the Park. M
 usic by Train Wreck Junction.\n\nPenngrove Parade – 50th annual parade 
 \n\n“The Biggest Little Parade in Northern California” Sunday\, July 5
 \, 2026 11 a.m. sharp - Parade on Downtown Penngrove on Main Street\n\nFre
 e to Enter - entries due July 1\n\nNoon – 4 pm – BBQ and music by **T
 rain Wreck Junction** in Penngrove Park\, 11800 Main St.\, Penngrove 949
 51. \n\n**Theme:** \n\n**Stars\, Stripes\, and A Parade!** \n\nCelebrate 
 50 & 250 Years at the Penngrove Parade\n\nIt's as small-town America as yo
 u can get. You’ll see tractors\, horses\, floats\, antique military Jee
 ps\, bands\, and bicycle teams. And\, it's blissfully under one hour!\n\n
 The menu offers old-fashioned pit beef\, BBQ chicken\, beef sandwiches\, o
 ysters\, and hot dogs. Drinks and Lagunitas beer will keep you cool. You
 ’ll want to visit the Penngrove 4-H dessert and cold soda booth. Purchas
 e barbecue tickets at the door.\n\n Grand Marshal Ray Soper will lead the
  parade in an historic fire engine. Soper has been involved with Penngrove
  Social Firemen for decades and is a past president. ​ **Know Before You
  Go:** Sorry\, no dogs\, coolers\, outside food or drink in the park. No 
 digital ID will be accepted. Bring cash or use the on-site ATM.  ​ This
  is the biggest annual fundraiser hosted by Penngrove Social Firemen\, a 
 non-profit 501(c)(3)\, to benefit the Penngrove community.\n\nFunds help m
 aintain the Penngrove Clubhouse and Penngrove Park\, and support local gro
 ups. Parade entry forms are available at Penngrove Market or online at  w
 ww.penngrovesocialfiremen.org. Entries must be received at Penngrove Mark
 et no later than Wednesday\, July 1st\, by 8 PM\, or emailed to mrsjjav
 a@hotmail.com.\n\nPhone (707) 318-2191\n\n Stay in touch at:\n\nhttps://
 www.penngrovesocialfiremen.org\n\nhttps://www.facebook.com/groups/33934794
 0599\n\nhttps://www.instagram.com/penngrovesocialfiremen/\n\n**July 5\, 20
 26** - Rancho Adobe Firefighters Association will be presenting the panca
 ke breakfast on July 5 at 4h 2026 from 0700-1100. This event is free to t
 he community and donations are accepted. For information\, contact Morgan
  DeJong\, mdejong@rafd.org.
LOCATION:Penngrove Park
URL:https://www.penngrovesocialfiremen.org
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Wine Tails Trail at Cuvaison Winery
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260705T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260705T170000
UID:260508HlzKzTwKZUCeiWzgql9pHw
DESCRIPTION:Enjoy a new way to experience Cuvaison with your canine compan
 ion on the Wine Tails Trail. This self-guided vineyard walk winds just und
 er a mile through our Los Carneros estate\, with QR code stops highlightin
 g the history of our vines and winemaking. Guests begin their adventure by
  checking in with our Concierge for a map and orientation before setting o
 ff on the trail.\n\nAfter the walk\, return to the estate and enjoy a seat
 ed tasting of our current release wines\, while your pup relaxes by your s
 ide and enjoys a selection of “Barkuterie.” The Wine Tails Trail is a 
 chance to stretch your legs\, explore the vineyard\, and savor Cuvaison in
  the company of your best friend.\n\nWhen booking this experience\, please
  plan for the dog walk to begin at the time you select. The walk itself av
 erages about 45 minutes\, though you’ll also check in with our Concierge
  before and after\, as well as complete a quick waiver at the start. Your 
 wine tasting will be scheduled 60 minutes after your selected walk time\, 
 allowing a smooth transition from the trail back to your seated experience
 .\n\nGroup Size: Up to 4 guests\, including non-tasters\n\nDuration: Pleas
 e allow 120 minutes for this experience
LOCATION:Cuvaison Experience Salon\, Outdoors Only
URL:https://tewines.com/pages/cuvaison-tastings 
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
