DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260705T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260705T170000
UID:260502In3PVp9C60WGftK53W20pw
DESCRIPTION:This summer\, Music in Place and the City of Sonoma invite you
  to soak up the sunshine\, sip local wine\, and dance to live music at the
  Sonoma Plaza Grinstead Amphitheater during Sonoma Sundays On the Plaza\, 
 a free concert series running June 7 through October 4\, 2026.\n\nThis wee
 k's lineup features Dirty Cello! Cello like you’ve never heard before! C
 ombine the virtuosic wail of Jimi Hendrix\, the soul of BB King\, and the 
 fire of Bill Monroe\, and add a whole lot of cello\, and you get the Dirty
  Cello band. With wild vocals\, and world class cello playing\, the group 
 is led by vivacious cross-over cellist\, Rebecca Roudman.\n\nSonoma Sunday
 s are free and open to all\, thanks to the generous support of the Sonoma 
 Community Center\, The Dawn Redwoods Trust\, and the McNeely Family Founda
 tion.\n\nPack your picnic\, bring your dancing shoes\, and meet us on the 
 Plaza!
LOCATION:Grinstead Amphitheater
URL:https://musicinplace.org/event/sonoma-sundays-on-the-plaza-7-5/
