BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Kids Scuba Camp
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260707T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260707T133000
UID:2606099MDNFJRDJUaazUCv6j04Jg
DESCRIPTION:At Pinnacles Dive Center\, our camps are designed to provide a
  safe and fun training program for kids interested in what lies beneath th
 e sea! A great way to reinforce water safety! Participants will also gain 
 skills and knowledge in Skin Diving Equipment Usage\, Ocean Environmental 
 Concerns and Marine Life. In addition\, participants will be given the opp
 ortunity to Scuba Dive in our 12' deep pool under the guidance of a profes
 sional Scuba Instructor.
LOCATION:Pinnacles Dive Center
URL:https://bayareascubadiving.com/courses/scuba-camp
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:TAKE YOUR TIME: Oil Pintings by Sharon Eisley
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260707T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260707T170000
UID:260529jcm5dfeIPkSEGAK2ZXSvLQ
DESCRIPTION:“Take Your Time”\n\nChange and transformation take time. I
 n her newest oil paintings Sharon Eisley explores the time as a process. B
 e it moving through grief\, re-framing your story of self\, or birthing so
 me new creation\, each painting lures you in with beautiful application th
 en holds you in time for a closer examination of our human experience. Eis
 ley's paintings are all inspired by tarot cards and her personal journey. 
 Tarot readings will be offered at the reception by @SymbolWarehouse for an
  optional small donation.\n\nOur guest artist\, Robert Benson\, will be ch
 allenging your eyes to fill in the details with his impressionist watercol
 ors.\n\nThis June 20th reception will be the FINAL art opening for Sebasto
 pol Gallery in its home of almost 20 years! This show may last only throug
 h June 2026\, then move to our new location. Or it may be up through June 
 and July. Either way\, this will be your last chance to come celebrate our
  local\, amazing group of artists at 150 N Main St.. “Take Your Time” 
 is a reminder to our collective to take our time finding and setting up ou
 r new home for all of you. I hope you can all come celebrate all the time 
 and art we shared with you in our lovely gallery.\n\nwww.sharoneisley.com
LOCATION:Sebastopol Gallery
URL:http://sebastopolgallery.com
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Wine Tails Trail at Cuvaison Winery
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260707T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260707T170000
UID:260508saxFHDBF2k-0qnMkVYvvrA
DESCRIPTION:Enjoy a new way to experience Cuvaison with your canine compan
 ion on the Wine Tails Trail. This self-guided vineyard walk winds just und
 er a mile through our Los Carneros estate\, with QR code stops highlightin
 g the history of our vines and winemaking. Guests begin their adventure by
  checking in with our Concierge for a map and orientation before setting o
 ff on the trail.\n\nAfter the walk\, return to the estate and enjoy a seat
 ed tasting of our current release wines\, while your pup relaxes by your s
 ide and enjoys a selection of “Barkuterie.” The Wine Tails Trail is a 
 chance to stretch your legs\, explore the vineyard\, and savor Cuvaison in
  the company of your best friend.\n\nWhen booking this experience\, please
  plan for the dog walk to begin at the time you select. The walk itself av
 erages about 45 minutes\, though you’ll also check in with our Concierge
  before and after\, as well as complete a quick waiver at the start. Your 
 wine tasting will be scheduled 60 minutes after your selected walk time\, 
 allowing a smooth transition from the trail back to your seated experience
 .\n\nGroup Size: Up to 4 guests\, including non-tasters\n\nDuration: Pleas
 e allow 120 minutes for this experience
LOCATION:Cuvaison Experience Salon\, Outdoors Only
URL:https://tewines.com/pages/cuvaison-tastings 
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Culinary Arts Camp at Hanna Center
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260707T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260707T160000
UID:260508MxXjnOqXXUWxpdH1RMb-bQ
DESCRIPTION:Ready to get cooking? Join Chef Courtney Clifton for a hands
 -on culinary experience where campers will learn to prepare delicious dish
 es\, from savory meals to sweet treats! This camp will teach basic cooking
  skills\, kitchen safety\, and fun techniques for preparing food. Each day
 \, campers will create and enjoy new recipes\, explore different cuisines\
 , and develop a love for cooking.
LOCATION:Hanna Center Cafeteria Kitchen
URL:https://hannacenter.org/services/community/camps/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Festival Napa Valley Presents LMR Jazz Orchestra
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260707T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260707T193000
UID:260428ID8QyG1SOke-q3OIBISdHw
DESCRIPTION:The LMR Jazz Orchestra returns to Festival Napa Valley with
  A Vanguard Legacy\, a tribute to the groundbreaking Thad Jones/Mel Lewis
  Orchestra\, whose weekly performances at New York’s Village Vanguard re
 shaped modern big-band jazz.\n\nThe evening is led by trumpet legend Jon F
 addis\, who joins the orchestra as both guest conductor and featured soloi
 st. Faddis served as lead trumpeter of the Thad Jones/Mel Lewis Orchestra 
 in the early 1970s beginning at just 18\, bringing a direct and vibrant li
 nk to the ensemble’s storied history. Vocalist Jamie Davis appears in th
 e celebrated baritone role long associated with Joe Williams\, revisiting 
 repertoire from the orchestra’s landmark recordings.\n\nFrom the driving
  pulse of “Low Down” to the enduring lyricism of “A Child Is Born\,
 ” the program highlights the sophistication\, swing\, and daring that de
 fined a jazz institution\, and keeps its spirit very much alive.\n\nWine\,
  beer\, and non-alcoholic beverages will be available for purchase from CI
 A at Copia. Outside food and beverages are not permitted.\n\nFestival Nap
 a Valley is committed to making concerts affordable for all with the intro
 duction of Choose Your Price. Choose the ticket price that feels right for
  you. Select the minimum amount\, the suggested amount\, or choose to cont
 ribute more to support the Festival's year-round Arts for All programs.\
 n\nCo-Presented with the Culinary Institute of America at Copia.
LOCATION:Jackson Family Wines Amphitheater at CIA at Copia
URL:https://festivalnapavalley.org/calendar/festival-live-lmr-jazz-orchest
 ra/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Beginner Salsa - Tuesdays
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260707T173000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260707T183000
UID:2603199cYnATmkvU600UkvBisdew
DESCRIPTION:Ready to dance? Join our beginner salsa class where no experie
 nce or partner is needed. Just comfortable shoes and desire to have fun!\n
 \nGreat for first timers!\n\nNo dance experience required\n\nNon-marking s
 hoes soles\n\nNo partner necessary\n\nOur relaxed environment is perfect f
 or learning salsa basics\, as we make it fun and enjoyable. In this class 
 you will learn basic directional steps\, proper frame for partner-work and
  simple turn patterns. We organize our curriculum so that the movements ar
 e easy to remember. Join us to learn the fundamentals! No experience is ne
 cessary and no partner is required. Drop-in fee is $20.\n\nDate & Time: Tu
 esdays @ 5:30PM – 6:30PM\n\nAddress: 4140 Redwood Highway \\#8 San Rafae
 l\, CA\n\nNote: Arrive 10 minutes before. No floor marking shoe soles allo
 wed.
LOCATION:Salsa Dance Marin
URL:https://www.pressdemocrat.com/events/#/details/beginner-salsa-tuesdays
 /17157360/2026-07-07T17
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Intermediate Salsa Class
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260707T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260707T193000
UID:2603184NtWWglePEuPt5PHGH_yaw
DESCRIPTION:This class is designed for dancers who have a solid grasp of t
 he basics and are eager to expand their repertoire with more complex and f
 luid movements.\n\nPre- requisite:\n\nSalsa Class Beginners\n\nEach week\,
  we’ll break down a new move\, focusing on the technique and connection 
 that will make you a more confident and stylish dancer. We’ll go beyond 
 the foundational steps to cover a wide range of essential intermediate pat
 terns and styling\, including:\n\nTurns and Spins:\n\nMaster your inside a
 nd outside turns\, double spins\, and the elegant 360 and Hand Toss moves.
 \n\nIntricate Patterns:\n\nLearn to execute the 360\, wrap\, as well as va
 rious Cross Body Lead variations like the U-Turn and Spiral.\n\nFootwork a
 nd Styling:\n\nEnhance your rhythm and flair with advanced footwork like t
 he Suzy Q\, Front Tap\, and Mambo Step. We’ll also work on styling with 
 a wrap and improving your posture and upper body movement.\n\nThis class i
 s your chance to refine your technique\, improve your lead-follow connecti
 on\, and add a variety of fun and dynamic moves to your salsa vocabulary. 
 Join us and elevate your dance!\n\nDetails:\n\nNo partner necessary — ro
 tations ensure everyone gets to dance.\n\nPlease wear non-marking shoe so
 les to protect the floor.\n\nArrive 10 minutes early to warm up and get s
 ettled.\n\nDate & Time: Tuesdays @ 6:30PM – 7:30PM
LOCATION:Salsa Dance Marin
URL:https://www.pressdemocrat.com/events/#/details/intermediate-salsa-clas
 s/17159571/2026-07-07T18
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
