BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Art Exhibit: Local Color
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260711T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260711T180000
UID:260616xzgUN56EDkm7lGA73zlT3g
DESCRIPTION:Date: FOR IMMEDIATE RELEASE  6/15/26\n\n**JULY EXHIBIT: LOC
 AL COLOR**\n\nEXHIBIT DATES:  **June 29 – July 26\, 2026**\n\n**RECEPT
 ION: SATURDAY\, July 4\, 2026\, 3-6 pm: Join us to meet Linda Barretta  
 and Gallery artists\;  Learn about their art and celebrate the show.  
 Be sure to take part in the Gallery’s free monthlong drawing for a beaut
 iful work by a Gallery artist.  Refreshments will be served.**\n\nSonoma
  County artist\, **Linda Barretta** presents **Local Color\,** a collecti
 on unveiling new oil paintings that tap into the vivid natural hues found 
 in our region’s breathtaking beauty.  From flowers to vineyards\, colo
 r takes a starring role in these works.  The deep purple hills in “Sun
 flower Daze” intensify the golden sweep of the sunflowers.  A peach tr
 ee celebrates the season with a glorious pink floral display in “Spring 
 Blooms.”  In “Winery Farm and Gardens\,” framed through a natural 
 arch of trees\, a sunlit vineyard draws the viewer.  “We are so fortun
 ate to live in Sonoma wine country – it’s stunning beauty is a daily i
 nspiration to pick up my brushes and paint\,” commented Barretta. \n\nL
 iving in Healdsburg\, Sonoma wine country is Barretta’s homebase.  She
  developed her impressionist style and skills through numerous hours of pl
 ein air painting and studying with master artists.  When Barretta create
 s the composition\, she is observing the play of light and colors that wil
 l highlight the compelling quality of the scene.  Her aim is to translat
 e her inspiration to the viewer.  From the rough sketch to the final bru
 shstroke\, this is the task she loves.  Barretta participates in the Art
  Trails Open Studio program and her works are exhibited regionally and thr
 oughout the country\,\n\nMeet the artist: Barretta will host the Gallery o
 n July 4\, 6 & 26\, 2:30 – 6pm and July 22\, 11am to 2:30 pm.\n\nThe Sta
 irway Smallworks Showcase features **Beverly Bird’s Birds by Bird\,** a
  collection of acrylic paintings that depict our feathered friends\, big a
 nd small\, in natural habitats.  Rendered in an impressionistic textured
  style\, these works imbue their subjects with a lively spirit.  Bald ea
 gles leave the viewer awed with their regal presence.  While the Steller
  and Scrub jays jauntily hint at their quirky character. In “Circling th
 e Light” the viewer joins a flock of geese on its migratory path. “Bir
 ds enliven our daily existence and their wild spirit provides endless subj
 ect matter\,” Bird noted of her inspiration for the series.\n\nMeet the 
 artist: Bird will host the Gallery on July 22 & 27\, 2:30 – 6pm and July
  29\, 11am to 6 pm.\n\nAlso join us for **ART NITE HEALDSBURG**\, Thursday
 \, July 2\, 5 – 7 pm.  ART NITE Healdsburg\, held the 1st Thursday of
  Every Month\, is a community event celebrating art and creativity with ov
 er 20 galleries participating.  ArtNiteHealdsburg.com.\n\nUpstairs Art G
 allery\, 306 Center Street\, Healdsburg\, CA 95448. (707) 431-4214.: OPEN 
 DAILY: 11am – 6 pm.    **www.upstairsart gallery.net** \n\nFor furt
 her information: Contact: Beverly Bird\, Press Contact\, at bvdrio@sonic.
 net or 707-799-1490.
LOCATION:Upstairs Art Gallery
URL:http://www.upstairsartgallery.net
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Summer Aliveness: Contemplative Practices for Joy\, Balance & Resi
 lience
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260711T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260711T153000
UID:260616aivcSH4OjkyNmEte5CsYcg
DESCRIPTION:with Elissa Epel\, PhD and Eve Ekman\, PhD\n\nHeld within the 
 fullness of summer\, this workshop offers a chance to pause in the richnes
 s of being alive amid the complexity of our lives and the world. Through c
 ontemplative practice and guided restoration\, we create space to soften\,
  listen\, and return to the senses—and to our innate capacity for love.\
 n\nBlending contemplative practice with contemporary science\, this daylon
 g workshop explores how emotional awareness supports resilience\, vitality
 \, and meaningful connection. We engage in practices that cultivate awaren
 ess\, connection\, and positive emotional states that support nervous syst
 em regulation\, enhanced allostasis\, and adaptability. Through meditation
 \, breathwork\, and reflection\, we’ll explore how resilience includes m
 oving gently through sadness and frustration while savoring the many joys 
 abundantly present in life.\n\nThis work is not about striving toward a di
 stant goal. It is about learning how to be here—steady\, responsive\, an
 d open-hearted—amidst a complex and changing world.
LOCATION:Spirit Rock Meditation Center
URL:https://spirit-rock.secure.retreat.guru/program/summer-aliveness-conte
 mplative-practices-for-joy-emotional-balance-and-deep-resilienceee2d26/?la
 ng=en
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Cuban Salsa Intermediate Workshop
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260711T150000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260711T163000
UID:26061296CETK7_602HmJicleT8aQ
DESCRIPTION:Take your dancing to the next level in this focused\, high-ene
 rgy intensive!\n\nDesigned for dancers who already know the fundamentals\,
  this special 90-minute cuban salsa workshop will move beyond basic steps 
 to focus on complex partner work patterns\, advanced body styling\, dynami
 c musicality\, and the authentic flow of Cuban Casino.\n\n• Format: 1-Da
 y Intensive Workshop \\(90 Minutes\\) • Date: Saturday\, July 11 • Tim
 e: 3:00 PM – 4:30 PM • Location: 4140 Redwood Highway \\#8\, San Rafae
 l\, CA • Registration Note: This workshop requires a minimum of 8 regist
 rations to run. Please register early so we can secure the session!\n\nPre
 requisites To ensure a fluid\, fast-paced learning environment\, this is a
 n Intermediate level workshop.\n\nRequirement: You must have completed a B
 eginner Cuban Salsa course or have a solid grasp of beginner fundamentals 
 \\(including basic footwork\, timing\, standard left/right turns\, and fun
 damental partner connection\\).\n\nWhat We Will Cover • Advanced Partner
 work: Intricate Cuban Casino patterns\, seamless transitions\, and directi
 onal changes. • Styling & Body Movement: Incorporating authentic Cuban b
 ody isolation and natural expression into your dancing. • Musicality & C
 onnection: Refining lead/follow mechanics to hit musical breaks and accent
 s naturally. • Intensive Structure: We will kick off with a quick body i
 solation warm-up and advanced footwork exercises before diving straight in
 to partnerwork technique and practical\, social-ready combinations.\n\nCom
 e dance with us\, elevate your technique\, and experience the energy and f
 lavor of Cuba in a supportive and welcoming environment!\n\nImportant Deta
 ils • Arrival: Please arrive 10 minutes before class starts \\(2:50 PM\\
 ) to check in. • Shoe Policy: No floor-marking shoe soles allowed on the
  dance floor.\n\nSaturday\, July 11 • 3:00 PM – 4:30 PM • 4140 Redwo
 od Highway \\#8\, San Rafael\, CA
LOCATION:Salsa Dance Marin
URL:https://salsadancemarin.com/cuban-salsa-intermediate-workshop/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
