BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Petaluma Art & Garden Festival
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260712T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260712T170000
UID:260518Ol9h7V6UA0Sw7A04HuH-wA
DESCRIPTION:The 23rd Art & Garden Festival\, one of Petaluma’s most che
 rished summer traditions\, is a vibrant\, family-friendly celebration of c
 reativity\, community\, and local flavor\, drawing crowds of over 15\,000
  people to historic downtown Petaluma to enjoy art\, music\, food\, and f
 un.\n\nExplore more than 100 handpicked art exhibitors offering unique\, h
 igh-quality\, handmade goods—from garden and home décor to artisan jewe
 lry and fine art. Live music will fill the air from two stages\, while loc
 al wineries\, breweries\, distilleries\, and restaurants serve up deliciou
 s tastes of Sonoma County and beyond. Gardening experts will be available 
 to share tips specific to local needs and conditions. The Children’s Cor
 ner features jump houses\, face painting\, and free hands-on arts and craf
 ts.\n\nThe festival takes place on Kentucky Street\, Fourth Street\, B Str
 eet\, and the A Street parking lot. Festival Headquarters will be locate
 d at the Petaluma Historical Library & Museum Garden Court\, 20 Fourth St
 reet.\n\nAdmission is free\, with tasting packages available for sampling 
 the amazing variety of wine\, craft beer\, cider\, cocktails\, and more.
LOCATION:Historic Downtown Petaluma
URL:https://petalumadowntown.com/art-garden.html
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Sonoma Sundays on the Plaza - Heidi Evelyn & the Savoy Sweethearts
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260712T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260712T170000
UID:260502TpiIRHHkk0a1PzOBVNJFcg
DESCRIPTION:This summer\, Music in Place and the City of Sonoma invite you
  to soak up the sunshine\, sip local wine\, and dance to live music at the
  Sonoma Plaza Grinstead Amphitheater during Sonoma Sundays On the Plaza\, 
 a free concert series running June 7 through October 4\, 2026.\n\nThis wee
 k's lineup features Heidi Evelyn and the Savoy Sweethearts! If you love to
  swing out to hot riffs or swoon to sweet melodies\, the Savoy Sweethearts
  are the band for you. They uniquely capture the sound of the late 1930s a
 nd early 1940s\, at the birth of the swing era and the lindy hop craze. Th
 e band features a roster of jazz masters with a passion for historical aut
 henticity\, powered by a true sense of rhythm and drive. The band features
  a blend of vintage arrangements and spontaneous creativity.\n\nSonoma Sun
 days are free and open to all\, thanks to the generous support of the Sono
 ma Community Center\, The Dawn Redwoods Trust\, and the McNeely Family Fou
 ndation.\n\nPack your picnic\, bring your dancing shoes\, and meet us on t
 he Plaza!
LOCATION:Grinstead Amphitheater
URL:https://musicinplace.org/event/sonoma-sundays-on-the-plaza-7-12/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
