BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Overeaters Anonymous (OA) Newcomer Meeting in Santa Rosa
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260712T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260712T170000
UID:260212wKN0oxgCsEWTDmiEZcfrMw
DESCRIPTION:Is Food a Problem for You? You Are Not Alone.\n\nOvereaters An
 onymous \\(OA\\) is a fellowship of people who support each other in recov
 ering from compulsive eating and food behaviors. If you feel you have a pr
 oblem with food\, OA welcomes you—no matter what your background\, belie
 fs\, or eating habits.\n\nWe hold an in-person newcomer meeting on Sundays
  from 4:00 – 5:00 PM at Christ Church United Methodist\, 1717 Yulupa Ave
 .\, Room \\#4\, Santa Rosa. Contact: Abigail \\(707\\) 293-5888. You may v
 iew all North Bay OA in-person and online meetings at https://www.northbay
 oa.org/meetings.html .\n\nIn OA\, members experience spiritual\, emotional
 \, and physical recovery by practicing the Twelve Steps and living by thei
 r spiritual principles—one day at a time.\n\nOA is not a diet club or ca
 lorie-counting program.\n\nMembers have different plans of eating.\n\nOA d
 oes not endorse any specific food plan.\n\nIf food is causing problems in 
 your life\, you don’t have to struggle alone. Recovery is possible\, and
  help is available.\n\nVisit: https://www.northbayoa.org/\n\nFind a meetin
 g: https://www.northbayoa.org/meetings.html
LOCATION:Christ Church United Methodist
URL:https://www.northbayoa.org/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Petaluma River History Paddle
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260712T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260712T120000
UID:260129DV5tzrIUj0aLRWJhH457Ww
DESCRIPTION:Enjoy a uniquely Petaluma experience on the water. This two-ho
 ur\, gentle guided kayak tour launches from The Floathouse Petaluma and ex
 plores the river that once served as the region's "saltwater highway." Lon
 g before roads and railways\, the Petaluma River powered San Francisco\, t
 he Gold Rush miners\, and even global markets with the produce from local 
 farms and industries\, supplying everything from eggs to overalls.\n\nDesi
 gned and led by a Petaluman\, actor and former history teacher this entert
 aining and enlightening tour brings history to life through storytelling e
 nhanced by costumed actors on shore. You'll hear fascinating stories from 
 the perspectives of long-ago Petalumans—young workers\, entrepreneurs\, 
 and colorful characters whose daily lives revolved around the river.\n\nPa
 ddle in stable sit-on-top kayaks through and beyond Petaluma's charming do
 wntown\, while gaining a deeper appreciation for how this tidal waterway s
 haped the city and the region. Visitors are often surprised by how much th
 ey learn—and many come back with friends.\n\n$75 per person\, all-inclus
 ive. No paddling experience necessary. All equipment provided.
LOCATION:The Floathouse Petaluma
URL:https://www.pressdemocrat.com/events/#/details/petaluma-river-history-
 paddle/17975629/2026-07-12T10
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The doRiaN Mode - Jazz Music
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260712T140000
