BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Comedy of Cliff Cash
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260716T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260716T213000
UID:260531PIxsZTDb1ESJTjTaJo9H0w
DESCRIPTION:Cliff tackles everything from racism to homophobia\, from gree
 d and war to death and dicorce saying \, "I believe it is our duty as comi
 cs to shine the light of levity into the dark corners of the human experie
 nce\, and by doing so we can take power away from the thngs that sadden or
  scare us.  Maybe that old saying about laughter being the best medicine r
 eally is true. I hope so because I don't have health insurance."\n\nCliff 
 Cash got his comedy start in Wilmington\, NC at Nutt St. Comedy\, now Dead
  Crow Comedy Room.  In the years since\, has has gone on to win Port city'
 s Top Comic\, Comedy Zones' almost famous\, and Bes of the Fest at SLO Com
 edy Festival\, and he has been a finalist n Comedy Central's UpNext and St
 andup NBV.  He's played iconic rooms from the Comedy Store n LA to the Com
 edy Cellar in New York City.  He's also headlines festivals like Altercati
 on Comedy Festival in Austin and Tree Fort Festival in Boise.  Cliff has b
 een featured on Sirius XM Comedy Central\, Rawdog\, Laughs TV\, Roftop Com
 edy\, and has a half-hour special from Dry Bar.  His 2021 debut album Half
 way There \\(released through StandUp! Records\\) spent a week at number o
 ne on iTunes. \n\nThis is a fundraiser for Sebastiani Theatre and Wake UP 
 Sonoma\n\nDoors open at 7:00. 
LOCATION:Sebastiani Theatre
URL:https://mynorthbaytickets.ticketsauce.com/e/the-comedy-of-cliff-cash?a
 ff=cityspark
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:TAKE YOUR TIME: Oil Pintings by Sharon Eisley
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260716T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260716T170000
UID:260529c3_XHpp890C04SvhSOmj0w
DESCRIPTION:“Take Your Time”\n\nChange and transformation take time. I
 n her newest oil paintings Sharon Eisley explores the time as a process. B
 e it moving through grief\, re-framing your story of self\, or birthing so
 me new creation\, each painting lures you in with beautiful application th
 en holds you in time for a closer examination of our human experience. Eis
 ley's paintings are all inspired by tarot cards and her personal journey. 
 Tarot readings will be offered at the reception by @SymbolWarehouse for an
  optional small donation.\n\nOur guest artist\, Robert Benson\, will be ch
 allenging your eyes to fill in the details with his impressionist watercol
 ors.\n\nThis June 20th reception will be the FINAL art opening for Sebasto
 pol Gallery in its home of almost 20 years! This show may last only throug
 h June 2026\, then move to our new location. Or it may be up through June 
 and July. Either way\, this will be your last chance to come celebrate our
  local\, amazing group of artists at 150 N Main St.. “Take Your Time” 
 is a reminder to our collective to take our time finding and setting up ou
 r new home for all of you. I hope you can all come celebrate all the time 
 and art we shared with you in our lovely gallery.\n\nwww.sharoneisley.com
LOCATION:Sebastopol Gallery
URL:http://sebastopolgallery.com
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
