BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:History Talks - Old Time Shopping
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260718T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260718T113000
UID:260623egBDkMVjOkCOCoF-4_wttQ
DESCRIPTION:Family-Owned Stores & Neighborhood Groceries\n\nSpeakers: Lill
 ie Deas and Meredith Dreisback\n\nFrom the 1930s to the 1960s\, Healdsburg
  was filled with small\, family-owned stores and markets offering resident
 s everything they needed. Small grocery stores were scattered around town 
 and everybody had a favorite\, often the one just an easy bike ride away f
 or the kids. And you could find a plethora of stores offering other produc
 ts like medical prescriptions\, clothing\, cigars\, phonograph records\, s
 hoes\, candy\, hardware….you name it.\n\nCome with us and we’ll take y
 ou shopping the old-fashioned way.
LOCATION:Healdsburg Plaza Gazebo
URL:https://www.healdsburgmuseum.org/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Redwood Writers General Meeting - Jordan Rosenfeld
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260718T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260718T133000
UID:260622yikpMQKV9Ei4W5MquIITsg
DESCRIPTION:**Jordan Rosenfeld: When the Character is You – Curating a P
 ersona in Memoir**\n\nPlease bring something savory or sweet to share in o
 ur potluck!\n\nThis workshop helps memoirists takes control of the narrati
 ve through a powerful persona that balance writers’ roles as both narrat
 or telling the story\, a character in the story. Memoirs often deal with d
 ifficult\, personal and intimate material that has to be selectively shape
 d and revealed. Curating a persona allows you to control and mold your nar
 rative exactly as you want and still tell your truth. We’ll look at what
  it means to create a written persona\, to curate a voice that is a styliz
 ed\, narrative version of you\, and to be intentional with your truth at t
 he sentence level.\n\n**About the Presenter:**\n\nJordan Rosenfeld is auth
 or of the novels *Fallout*\, *Women in Red*\, and *Forged in Grace*\, a
 nd eight books on the craft of writing\, including the forthcoming *Writi
 ng Through the Pause: Mining Midlife for Powerful Writing*\, as well as *
 The Sound of Story: Developing Voice and Tone in Writing*\, *How to Write
  a Page-Turner*\, the bestselling *Make a Scene*\, *Writing the Intimate
  Character*\, *A Writer’s Guide to Persistence*\, *Writing Deep Scenes
 * (with Martha Alderson)\, and *Write Free* (with Rebecca Lawton). Her f
 reelance writing has been published in hundreds of publications\, includin
 g: The Atlantic\, The New York Times\, Publisher’s Weekly\, Salon\, Scie
 ntific American\, The Rumpus\, Writer’s Digest Magazine\, The Washington
  Post and many more. She is also a freelance manuscript editor\, writing c
 oach and teaches online classes.
LOCATION:Finley Center
URL:https://redwoodwriters.org/july-2026-jordan-rosenfeld/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Trail Crew Saturdays
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260718T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260718T130000
UID:260620LMHP8ZiiZUK6lDj8LQ-LxQ
DESCRIPTION:Volunteers play a crucial role at keeping Sugarloaf Ri
 dge State Park open and accessible to all! Help Sugarloaf with 
 trail restoration work by coming to our monthly Saturday Voluntee
 r Trail Crew\, 9:00 am-1:00 pm. Activities include bridge and st
 ep construction\, installing signs\, clearing\, lifting\, carrying\,
  and hiking. \n\nMeet at the White Barn. Bring gloves\, hat\, a
 nd water that you can carry hands-free \\(i.e. bring a backpack\
 \). Wear long pants\, boots or sturdy shoes and sunscreen. Long
  sleeves are suggested as poison oak is present. We have tools
  and trained crew leaders with tasks for all. Minors must be a
 ccompanied by a parent or legal guardian. We will provide tools
  and refreshments.
LOCATION:Sugarloaf Ridge State Park
URL:https://sec.regfox.com/julytrailsat26
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
