BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:JAD Experience presents LUNAE
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260718T173000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260718T220000
UID:2605199pWQ_e3SxUSnLwTUbq6i1w
DESCRIPTION:JAD Experience\, the trailblazing series uniting regenerative 
 cuisine and world-class ballet\, announces LUNAE\, its milestone 13th seas
 on. Taking place July 17–19 and July 24–26\, LUNAE is an immersive eve
 ning of farm-to-table dining\, world-class ballet under the stars\, and de
 ep connection with nature.\n\nInspired by the 13 lunar cycles of the year\
 , LUNAE’s choreography evokes the timeless rhythms of creation\, surrend
 er\, and renewal through themes of feminine energy\, light\, and shadow.\n
 \nPerched atop Tara Firma Farms \\(3796 I Street Ext.\, Petaluma\, CA 9495
 2\\) with sweeping pastoral views\, LLUNAE delivers on the original social
  ritual: shared culinary experience at long tables. Following dinner\, an 
 intimate ballet performance unfolds beneath the night sky for just 100 gue
 sts each evening.\n\nEvenings begin with arrival and cocktails from 5:30 t
 o 7 p.m.\, followed by dinner from 7 to 8:30 p.m. The experience continues
  with the ballet performance from 8:45 to 9:30 p.m.\, and the evening conc
 ludes at 10 p.m.\n\nFree parking is available\, and all seating offers exc
 ellent views of the open-air stage. Because evenings in Petaluma can cool 
 quickly\, guests are encouraged to bring warm layers\; blankets and hot ch
 ocolate will also be provided. Guests needing assistance may choose betwee
 n a hayride or a shuttle for accessibility.\n\nRenowned choreographer Juli
 a Adam\, an Ottawa native and former San Francisco Ballet principal dancer
  \\(1988–2002\\)\, has created more than 100 works for companies includi
 ng Houston Ballet and the National Ballet of Canada.\n\nFeatured dancers i
 nclude David O’matz \\(Pittsburgh Ballet Theatre\\)\, Augi Lehner\, Ryan
  Williams\, Saela Rivera-Martinez\, Zoe Lucich \\(Bay Area\, Houston Balle
 t\\)\, Harry Warshaw \\(Ballet Memphis\\)\, Lily Mangiaruga \\(New Orleans
  Ballet Theatre\\)\, Kelsey Mcfalls \\(freelance\, Bay Area\\)\, and Tessa
  Barbour \\(Smuin Ballet\, Bay Area\\).\n\nDinner is led by chefs Brian Le
 itner and Annette Yang of Pearl\, presenting a multi-course menu rooted in
  the farm and its surrounding network. The evening features dishes such as
  beef tartare\, summer succotash\, grilled strip loin\, and seasonal desse
 rts\, alongside substantial vegetarian and vegan offerings.\n\nIngredients
  are sourced transparently from Tara Firma Farms and regional partners\, i
 ncluding Umbel Roots\, Feed Sonoma\, True Grass Farms\, and Holistic Ag. B
 everage pairings include wines from Enkidu and Shokrian\, beers from HenHo
 use and Moonlight Brewing\, and house-made nonalcoholic options.\n\nTara F
 irma Farms\, a working cattle ranch stewarded by JAD co-founder Aaron Luci
 ch\, powers this chef-farmer artistry.\n\nIn an era shaped by screen addic
 tion and fleeting digital distractions\, LUNAE offers a return to genuine 
 human connection through live performance\, communal dining\, and an extra
 ordinary natural setting.\n\n“LUNAE follows thirteen lunar cycles\, with
  each phase shaping the timing and movement of the choreography\,” said 
 Julia Adam\, Co-Founder & Choreographer. “The work draws on feminine ene
 rgy\, expressed through exquisite motion\, repetition\, and release.” \
 n\n“We need to become conscious that we are just a part of the natural s
 ystem\,” said Aaron Lucich\, Co-Founder & Tara Firma Farms Managing Part
 ner. “Land and people heal together. LUNAE's farm-driven feasts at long 
 communal tables\, grown from our regenerative soils\, model this: dining a
 s unity\, ballet as connection\, all under the moon to remind us we're a p
 art of nature's own cycles.”
LOCATION:Tara Firma Farms
URL:https://jadexperience.org/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:World Premiere: The Judgment of Paris
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260718T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260718T200000
UID:260516HSjNW-PNmU2zbmp0dP_K4w
DESCRIPTION:Commissioned for Festival Napa Valley's 20th Anniversary Seaso
 n\, *The Judgment of Paris* is a one-act opera by composer Jake Heggie a
 nd librettist Gene Scheer\, inspired by the legendary 1976 blind tasting t
 hat transformed the world of wine.\n\nThe production features an exception
 al cast led by soprano Danielle De Niese\, baritone Quinn Kelsey\, tenor N
 icholas Phan\, and mezzo-sopranos Simone McIntosh and Brenda Rae. They are
  joined by the Manetti Shrem Opera Program Fellows and the Festival Orches
 tra Napa under the baton of Kent Nagano\, with stage direction by Jean-Rom
 ain Vesperini.\n\nElevate the experience with *The Judgment of Paris* Ope
 ra Tasting\, a celebration of Napa Valley wines for $85. Enjoy a pre-perfo
 rmance glass of Charles Krug and a curated charcuterie box. After the pr
 emiere\, join a celebratory reception featuring a tasting of wines from C
 hateau Montelena and Stag’s Leap Wine Cellars\, the wineries awarded t
 op honors at the 1976 Judgment of Paris\, along with special selections fr
 om Bouchaine Vineyards.
LOCATION:Charles Krug 
URL:https://www.pressdemocrat.com/events/#/details/world-premiere-the-judg
 ment-of-paris/18756529/2026-07-18T18
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:14th Annual Wine Country Yarn Hop
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260718T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260718T170000
UID:260514nGAu8VlnTEC46CDxIK4lGw
DESCRIPTION:Join us for the 14th annual Northern California yarn lovers ex
 perience from July 17-19\, 2026!\n\nThe Wine Country Yarn Hop consists of 
 5 shops located in the beautiful Wine Country between Petaluma & Ukiah.\n\
 nThe 2026 Yarn Hop is FREE and begins July 17\, 2026 at 10:00am. The Hop i
 s 3 days long\, you can choose to do all 5 shops in one day\, or spread it
  out and hop all weekend.\n\nAll 5 shops are open from 10:00 - 5:00 each d
 ay of the Hop: July 17\, 18 & 19.\n\nYou will receive a passport to be sta
 mped at each shop\, as well as 1 raffle ticket per stop. Participants will
  be entered to win a prize basket at each shop\, AND the Grand Prize baske
 t when a complete passport is turned in. FREE patterns\, and free enamel p
 ins w/ tote or lanyard purchase.\n\nNo need to register - just start hoppi
 ng at any of the 5 shops!\n\nLearn more: winecountryyarnhop.com\n\nPartici
 pating Shops:\n\nFiber Circle Studios- Petaluma\n\nNoma Knits- Sonoma \n\
 nCast Away Yarn Shop- Santa Rosa\n\nPurls of Joy- Healdsburg\n\nPurple Nee
 dle- Ukiah
LOCATION:Cast Away Yarn Shop
URL:https://winecountryyarnhop.com/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Summer Restorative Yoga
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260718T103000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260718T113000
UID:260427RVzi2F9mLEehQfxkEwwoDw
DESCRIPTION:Begin your summer Saturday mornings with a calming session of 
 restorative yoga at the Garden - an invitation to slow down\, breathe deep
 ly\, and reconnect with yourself in a peaceful natural setting. Whether yo
 u’re looking to unwind from a busy week or manage ongoing stress\, this 
 beginner-friendly class offers a gentle path toward physical and emotional
  balance. Join us to explore the deeply relaxing practices of Yoga Nidra\,
  Yin Yoga\, and restorative postures—all designed to release tension\, c
 alm the nervous system\, and support mindful rest. Classes take place indo
 ors in our Center for Learning & Engagement\, surrounded by the peaceful e
 nergy of the Garden\, it’s the perfect setting to unwind. Sessions are l
