 ottle of wine with charcuterie\, presented in a quintessential wicker bask
 et and a chic red wagon\, offering a relaxed and beautifully curated alfre
 sco wine country experience. Guests can enjoy their picnic in picturesque\
 , family- and dog-friendly settings across the estate—whether on the Pav
 ilion lawn\, beneath the trellis by the pond\, or at the picnic tables nes
 tled within the culinary and rose gardens. With exceptional wines\, thou
 ghtfully crafted foods\, and sweeping vistas\, a visit to Bricoleur Vin
 eyards offers a laid-back\, family-friendly atmosphere featuring lawn ga
 mes\, board games\, scavenger hunts\, and catch-and-release fishing.
LOCATION:Bricoleur Vineyard
URL:https://bricoleurvineyards.com/pages/visit?srsltid=AfmBOoq4MRc2MHal1tH
 0HwUmLbCHlVrPlsnizqNwrRFitw3UKui4rRJV
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:A Taste of Italy at Centennial Mountain Tasting Room
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260718T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260718T170000
UID:260430zjjDm-S6JUKkkUKxy1Pu1g
DESCRIPTION:For wine drinkers eager to experience world-class wines made i
 n California from Italian varieties\, the Centennial Mountain Tasting Room
  is a must during any trip to Sonoma County. Located just off the plaza in
  the charming town of Healdsburg near famed restaurants\, boutiques and ga
 lleries\, the Centennial Mountain Tasting Room is a destination that invit
 es discovery. Founded by the acclaimed team that guides renowned Pinot Noi
 r and Chardonnay producer Rhys Vineyards\, Centennial Mountain was establi
 shed to explore Italian grape varieties grown on its acclaimed Centennial 
 Mountain Vineyard in the rugged mountains of Northern Sonoma County.\n\nTh
 e Centennial Mountain Vineyard Tasting features the winery’s coveted Neb
 biolo\, and the pioneering Carricante and Nerello Mascalese wines\, among 
 others. To showcase how beautifully the wines pair with food\, the winery 
 also offers a delicious Wine and Sushi Pairing from nearby Asahi Sushi\, o
 ne of Healdsburg’s most popular dining destinations.\n\nGuests can also 
 enhance their tasting experience with a curated salumi board from Journeym
 an Meat Company. This generous accompaniment features six house-made salum
 i\, crostini\, cornichons\, olives\, and a selection of local cheese that 
 serves 2 to 5 guests.
LOCATION:Centennial Mountain Tasting Room
URL:https://cmvineyard.com/visit/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Sunset Spirit Sound Bath
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260718T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260718T200000
UID:260427thG5ebuO0EOCIQFHODel_w
DESCRIPTION:In celebration of our Spirit Guides exhibition\, join Glen El
 len–based practitioners Amelia Belle and Bob Rudorf for a restorative op
 en air sound bath inspired by the wisdom\, symbolism\, and grounding prese
 nce of the natural world. For over a decade\, Amelia and Bob have used sou
 nd and guided meditation as tools for transformation. In this immersive ex
 perience\, crystal singing bowls and other resonant instruments blend with
  the natural sounds of the Garden\, creating a meditative soundscape that 
 echoes the themes of Spirit Guides—connection\, reflection\, and inner a
 wakening. For this July 18 sound bath\, Amelia and Bob with be joined by r
 enown Ceremonial Sound Practitioner & Healing Performance Artist\, René J
 enkins. For more than 30 years\, René performs sound healing concerts\, b
 lessings and ceremonies for individuals and special groups throughout the 
 US and internationally. While embracing the ancestral wisdom from cross-cu
 ltural anthropologist Angeles Arrien\, Kashaya-Pomo elder/healer Lorin Smi
 th\, and renowned South American sound healer/musician Tito La Rosa\, Ren
 é raises consciousness-vibration through Sacred Sound and Intention. Held
  in the Garden’s outdoor grassy amphitheater at Sonoma Botanical Garden\
 , the session unfolds beneath the open sky as day transitions into evening
 . As you settle into stillness\, you’ll be gently bathed in calming freq
 uencies designed to quiet the mind\, relax the body\, and open the heart. 
 The vibrations of the crystal bowls move through you\, helping to release 
 tension\, restore balance\, and cultivate a deeper sense of presence. Open
  to all levels\, this experience invites you to reconnect with nature and 
 yourself—an opportunity to pause\, reflect\, and attune to the rhythms o
 f the living landscape.
LOCATION:Sonoma Botanical Garden
URL:https://sonomabotanicalgarden.ticketing.veevartapp.com/tickets/view/li
 st/sunset-spirit-sound-bath-700-pm-800-pm_1
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
