BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Historic Trees at Jack London State Historic Park
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260719T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260719T113000
UID:260622Jswdsjn30ku6p5Rw2w7Zlg
DESCRIPTION:Join a 2.5-mile guided walk along historic trails through Beau
 ty Ranch and down to the Wolf House ruins to explore the trees that helped
  shape Jack London’s property and vision for the land. Along the way\, l
 earn about London’s ambitious eucalyptus planting project\, heritage orc
 hard trees\, and other notable specimens that have been part of the ranch
 ’s landscape for generations.\n\nFrom the cottage gardens and Jack’s b
 eloved coast live oak to the remnants of the Wolf House orchard\, this lei
 surely walk reveals the rich natural and cultural history of Beauty Ranch 
 through its most iconic trees. Discover how these living landmarks reflect
  London’s agricultural experimentation\, landscape design\, and lasting 
 influence on the land.
LOCATION:Jack London State Historic Park
URL:https://jacklondonpark.com/events/historic-trees-of-beauty-ranch-2026/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Sonoma Creek Lower Headwaters Wildflower & Nature Hike
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260719T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260719T120000
UID:260619gNQaAt49hk2kpvvHplh6Wg
DESCRIPTION:Office hours without the office! Having bid farewell t
 o spring\, we will be looking for summer-blooming species includi
 ng larkspurs\, monkeyflowers\, clarkias\, and lilies\, and we will
  discuss the ecology of plant communities and how they respond 
 to geology\, fire\, human interventions\, and pollinators. Our rou
 te on the Lower Bald Mountain\, Meadow\, Hillside\, and Creekside
  Nature Trails highlights the park's diverse landscapes and natur
 al beauty while avoiding steep exposed climbs.\n\nMeet at the mai
 n parking lot. Tickets are $10 for general audiences\, $5 for s
 tudents\, youth \\(12-17 year olds must be accompanied by a pare
 nt or legal guardian\\)\, Sugarloaf  members\, Sugarloaf or RFO 
 volunteers\, and free for children under 12. Wear comfortable clo
 thing\, appropriate footwear for rocky/slippery trails\, and sun p
 rotection. Bring at least a quart of water\, hiking poles\, and
  if you desire\, a snack. Parking fees apply.
LOCATION:Sugarloaf Ridge State Park
URL:https://sec.regfox.com/sonoma-creek-lower-headwaters-wildflower-nature
 -hike-7192026
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Valley of the Moon Music Festival: In Shadow & Song (Concert 4)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260719T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260719T180000
UID:2606194dJpPa2RzkuKxxER9t96Uw
DESCRIPTION:Experience an afternoon of evocative chamber music inspired by
  Dvořák’s travels to Russia at the invitation of Tchaikovsky. This ric
 hly expressive program explores a vibrant musical world through works by A
 rensky\, Dvořák\, Mussorgsky\, and the long-overlooked composer Yuliya W
 eissberg. Concert duration: approximately 2 hours with intermission.\n\nTh
 e Valley of the Moon Music Festival returns July 11–26\, 2026\, with Pos
 tcards from Dvořák\, a season inspired by the travels\, influences\, and
  cultural connections behind the composer’s music. Set in the heart of S
 onoma Valley\, the festival brings together internationally acclaimed musi
 cians for historically informed performances that blend world-class classi
 cal music with the beauty and charm of wine country.
LOCATION:Hanna Center Auditorium
URL:https://valleyofthemoonmusicfestival.org/event/russia-in-shadow-song/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Summer Sundays Music Series at Montgomery Village
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260719T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260719T140000
UID:260618jobjXdAXw06FE3pqJXONbA
DESCRIPTION:Summer Sundays Music Series at Montgomery Village\n\nFree live
  music\, good vibes\, and a great excuse to make a Sunday out of it.\n\nSu
 mmer Sundays Music Series is a free monthly event bringing live music to t
 he Courtyard at Montgomery Village all summer long. This year\, we’re fe
 aturing local saxophonist Jimmy Galvan\, whose sound sets the perfect back
 drop for a relaxed afternoon in the heart of Sonoma County. Come for the m
 usic\, stay for the shopping\, dining\, coffee and ice cream. No tickets\,
  no fuss\, just a great community afternoon.\n\nJoin us on Sunday\, July 1
 9th from 12–2pm in the Courtyard at Montgomery Village (located near Mon
 ti’s\, Salt & Straw and Anthropologie). We invite you to grab a bite or 
 treat from your favorite Village restaurant or cafe\, then settle into the
  Courtyard and enjoy the sounds of summer. Summer Sundays are free and ope
 n to the community.
LOCATION:Montgomery Village
URL:https://montgomeryvillageca.com/event/summer-sundays-music-series-3/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
